MailableEmail builder <pre><code>&lt;?php

namespace App\Mails;

use Myth\Postal\Mailable;

class Welcome extends Mailable
{
    public function __construct(private readonly string $address)
    {
        parent::__construct();
    }

    protected function build(): void
    {
        $this-&gt;from('hello@example.com', 'Acme')
            -&gt;to($this-&gt;address)
            -&gt;subject('Welcome aboard')
            -&gt;markdown('emails/welcome');
    }
}

$result = (new Welcome('user@example.com'))-&gt;send();
</code></pre> <pre><code>&lt;?php

use Myth\Postal\Email;

$email = (new Email())
    -&gt;from('hello@example.com', 'Acme')
    -&gt;to('user@example.com')
    -&gt;subject('Welcome aboard')
    -&gt;html('&lt;p&gt;Glad to have you with us.&lt;/p&gt;');

$result = service('mailer')-&gt;send($email);
</code></pre> <p>Either way, <code>send()</code> returns a <code>SendResult</code> instead of a bare <code>bool</code>:</p> <pre><code>&lt;?php

if (! $result-&gt;success) {
    log_message('error', 'Welcome email failed: ' . $result-&gt;error);
}
</code></pre> <p>Out of the box Postal's default mailer discards every message, so nothing is sent by accident. The Quick Start sets up a mailer in a few lines.</p>
